.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KDIR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kdir
.Nd make a ZFS dataset where you would have made a directory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl p
.Op Fl o Ar property Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Ar path ...
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is
.Xr mkdir 1
for a ZFS system: for each
.Ar path
it creates a dataset mounted there, so the directory can have its own
snapshots, quota, compression and record size, and be sent, cloned and
rolled back on its own.
.Pp
The dataset is named under the dataset mounted at the path's parent:
with
.Pa /srv
mounted from
.Ql rpool/srv ,
.Ql kdir /srv/app
creates
.Ql rpool/srv/app ,
mounted at
.Pa /srv/app .
It then checks that the new dataset really is mounted at
.Ar path .
.Pp
It refuses, and creates nothing:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
a parent that is not where a dataset is mounted \(em a plain directory, or
not ZFS \(em unless
.Fl p ;
.It
a path that exists as a directory with files in it, which the dataset
would hide;
.It
a path where a dataset is already mounted;
.It
a relative path.
.El
.Pp
It must run as root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p
Create the missing parents as datasets too, from the top down.
A parent that exists as a plain directory is refused: it cannot become a
dataset without hiding what is in it.
.It Fl o Ar property Ns = Ns Ar value
Set a ZFS property on each dataset created; repeat for more.
A
.Ql mountpoint=
that differs from
.Ar path
is created and reported as an error, since the dataset is then not where
it was asked for.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Every path is a dataset now.
.It 1
Refused, not root, or
.Xr zfs 8
failed; paths before the failing one were created.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, under a throwaway dataset,
.Ql rpool/kd-3587274
mounted at
.Pa /var/tmp/kd-3587274 ,
that held a plain directory,
.Pa plain ;
all destroyed afterwards.
.Ss One dataset
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kdir /var/tmp/kd-3587274/good
kdir: creating dataset: rpool/kd-3587274/good  →  /var/tmp/kd-3587274/good
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Ss With its parents (-p)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kdir -p /var/tmp/kd-3587274/a/b/c
kdir: creating dataset: rpool/kd-3587274/a  →  /var/tmp/kd-3587274/a
kdir: creating dataset: rpool/kd-3587274/a/b  →  /var/tmp/kd-3587274/a/b
kdir: creating dataset: rpool/kd-3587274/a/b/c  →  /var/tmp/kd-3587274/a/b/c
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Ss With properties (-o)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kdir -o compression=zstd -o quota=1G /var/tmp/kd-3587274/z
kdir: creating dataset: rpool/kd-3587274/z  →  /var/tmp/kd-3587274/z
# (exited 0)
# zfs list -H -o name,mountpoint,compression,quota -r rpool/kd-3587274
rpool/kd-3587274	/var/tmp/kd-3587274	lz4	none
\&...
rpool/kd-3587274/good	/var/tmp/kd-3587274/good	lz4	none
rpool/kd-3587274/z	/var/tmp/kd-3587274/z	zstd	1G
.Ed
.Ss What it refuses
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kdir /var/tmp/kd-3587274/plain/data
kdir: error: parent '/var/tmp/kd-3587274/plain' is not where a ZFS dataset is mounted (a plain directory, or not ZFS); use -p to create it
# (exited 1)
# kdir -p /var/tmp/kd-3587274/plain/x
kdir: error: /var/tmp/kd-3587274/plain exists as a plain directory; kdir cannot make it a dataset (its files would be hidden)
# (exited 1)
# kdir /var/tmp/kd-3587274/good
kdir: error: /var/tmp/kd-3587274/good is already where a dataset is mounted
# (exited 1)
# kdir relative/path
kdir: error: 'relative/path' must be an absolute path
# (exited 1)
# kdir -o mountpoint=/var/tmp/kd-3587274/elsewhere /var/tmp/kd-3587274/m
kdir: creating dataset: rpool/kd-3587274/m  →  /var/tmp/kd-3587274/m
kdir: error: created rpool/kd-3587274/m, but it is mounted at /var/tmp/kd-3587274/elsewhere, not /var/tmp/kd-3587274/m (a -o mountpoint= overrides the path)
# (exited 1)
$ kdir /var/tmp/kd-3587274/u
kdir: error: must run as root (zfs create)
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mkdir 1 ,
.Xr zfsprops 7 ,
.Xr kclone 8 ,
.Xr kdf 8 ,
.Xr zfs-create 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: with a plain directory as the parent,
.Nm
named the new dataset after the dataset containing that directory, so it
was mounted somewhere else than it said \(em
.Ql kdir /x/plain/data
reported
.Pa /x/plain/data
and mounted at
.Pa /x/data ,
exit 0.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
A dataset's name follows the parent dataset's, not the path: under a
parent mounted somewhere unusual, the name can look unrelated to the
path.
